## Task Tracking

This project uses **bd (beads)** for issue tracking. Do not use GitHub Issues or
markdown TODO lists for day-to-day task tracking.

```bash
bd prime               # show full workflow context
bd ready               # find available work
bd show <id>           # view issue details
bd update <id> --claim # claim work
bd close <id>          # complete work
bd remember "insight"  # store persistent knowledge across sessions
```

Session close protocol before finishing a work session:

1. File issues for remaining work (`bd create`)
2. Run quality gates (`npm test`, `npm run validate:data`, `npm run build`)
3. Update or close the relevant issue (`bd update`, `bd close <id>`)

## Key Conventions

- **No backend, no database, no auth.** This is a static site. Don't propose
  server endpoints, sessions, or persistence beyond `localStorage`.
- **No framework islands.** No React/Vue/Svelte components for interactivity —
  vanilla `<script>` only. Prefer static generation over client-side rendering.
- **Tailwind v4 cannot build dynamic class names at runtime** — a variable-built
  `bg-[#hex]` fails silently. Use inline `style=` with `getSeriesMeta(seriesId).color`
  for dynamic series colors; opacity tint = hex suffix (`color + '20'` ≈ 12%).
- **Country codes are ISO alpha-2 only.** `countryFlag()` returns an empty string
  for alpha-3 input — always convert to alpha-2 at the data layer, not in the UI.
- **All stored/transmitted times are UTC** (`...Z` suffix). The browser localizes
  at render time via the `<LocalTime>` component — never format times manually in
  a component, hardcode an offset, or store local time in data files.
- **Session durations** come from `getSessionDurationMinutes()` in
  `src/lib/sessions.ts` — don't redefine duration maps elsewhere (UI helpers, ICS
  export, timelines, kiosk logic).
- Keep `/status` (the kiosk page) minimal — small screens, auto-refresh, no
  interactive chrome.

